1
00:00:01,921 --> 00:00:03,298
Hoo, hoo!

2
00:00:03,410 --> 00:00:04,337
Hi!

3
00:00:04,387 --> 00:00:06,415
It's me, Popcorn!

4
00:00:06,536 --> 00:00:11,767
Welcome to Popcorn Tales, the
cozy nest of bedtime stories.

5
00:00:12,079 --> 00:00:15,494
Hug your teddy, because
tonight's story is:

6
00:00:15,544 --> 00:00:17,767
The Boy Who Didn't Know Fear!

7
00:00:22,333 --> 00:00:26,005
Once upon a time, in a little
village at the foot of a hill,

8
00:00:26,055 --> 00:00:30,435
there lived a boy named Bruno, who
shared a house with his father and his

9
00:00:30,485 --> 00:00:31,685
older brother.

10
00:00:32,227 --> 00:00:37,802
Bruno was cheerful, curious and kind,
but there was one unusual thing about

11
00:00:37,852 --> 00:00:38,578
him:

12
00:00:38,628 --> 00:00:41,015
he still did not know what fear was.

13
00:00:41,630 --> 00:00:45,711
When the door of the house creaked
in the dark, his brother would jump,

14
00:00:45,797 --> 00:00:50,961
and Bruno would go to see what it
was, always with a smile on his face.

15
00:00:54,296 --> 00:00:57,162
Father, I have heard so
many people talk about fear,

16
00:00:57,212 --> 00:00:59,531
but I still do not know
what that feeling is,

17
00:00:59,581 --> 00:01:03,759
Bruno said, with his eyes
shining with curiosity.

18
00:01:04,322 --> 00:01:08,275
My son, everybody feels a tight
little jump in the chest sometimes,

19
00:01:08,325 --> 00:01:11,115
and I only wanted you to
be careful in the forest,

20
00:01:11,165 --> 00:01:15,759
the father said, worried,
but with great tenderness.

21
00:01:16,426 --> 00:01:20,853
On the fence post lived a brown
owl with a red bow on her head,

22
00:01:20,967 --> 00:01:23,284
who had been listening in silence.

23
00:01:23,865 --> 00:01:25,242
Hoo, hoo!

24
00:01:25,355 --> 00:01:30,566
If you want so much to learn, I will go
with you, because the world holds many

25
00:01:30,616 --> 00:01:34,252
strange things, and
also many funny things,

26
00:01:34,302 --> 00:01:37,258
Popcorn said, spreading her wings.

27
00:01:37,879 --> 00:01:41,932
Bruno squeezed his father's
hand, packed a loaf of bread,

28
00:01:41,990 --> 00:01:45,899
a piece of cheese and a lantern,
and set off down the road,

29
00:01:45,949 --> 00:01:48,529
with Popcorn flying beside him.

30
00:01:49,641 --> 00:01:54,758
They walked until the sun hid behind
the trees, and the forest grew quiet and

31
00:01:54,808 --> 00:01:56,624
silver with moonlight.

32
00:01:56,791 --> 00:02:01,685
The wind moved through the branches,
and far away, high in the trees,

33
00:02:01,735 --> 00:02:04,621
a soft night call drifted through the air.

34
00:02:07,516 --> 00:02:11,703
What a beautiful night, Popcorn, the
moon looks like a round cheese hanging in

35
00:02:11,753 --> 00:02:12,622
the sky,

36
00:02:12,672 --> 00:02:16,127
Bruno said, lifting his lantern with joy.

37
00:02:16,783 --> 00:02:21,538
Hoo, hoo, that is true, but
listen to that sound up ahead,

38
00:02:21,588 --> 00:02:24,564
because somebody is calling from far away,

39
00:02:24,614 --> 00:02:28,223
Popcorn said, turning her head with care.

40
00:02:35,008 --> 00:02:39,694
At the end of the path stood an old
stone church, and the bell in the tower

41
00:02:39,744 --> 00:02:44,158
was striking the hours of
the night, slowly and deeply.

42
00:02:45,248 --> 00:02:49,898
Bruno came up to the door, which
opened with a long old creak.

43
00:02:53,197 --> 00:02:57,800
In the entrance stood a man with grey
hair, wrapped in a white blanket because

44
00:02:57,850 --> 00:03:02,417
the night was cold, and he
smiled as soon as he saw the boy.

45
00:03:02,967 --> 00:03:06,806
Good evening, traveler, I am
the bell ringer of this church,

46
00:03:06,856 --> 00:03:10,417
and I was only ringing the bell, to
let everyone know that the night is

47
00:03:10,467 --> 00:03:11,692
already high,

48
00:03:11,742 --> 00:03:14,948
the bell ringer said, waving his lantern.

49
00:03:15,619 --> 00:03:20,222
Bruno let out a relieved and happy
laugh, because from far away the white

50
00:03:20,272 --> 00:03:24,972
blanket had almost looked like a ghost,
and up close it was only a man who

51
00:03:25,022 --> 00:03:26,311
felt cold.

52
00:03:26,942 --> 00:03:31,128
I left home to learn what fear was, and
for a second I almost felt something,

53
00:03:31,178 --> 00:03:33,271
but now I only want to
help you with the bell,

54
00:03:33,321 --> 00:03:37,096
Bruno said, already
climbing the tower stairs.

55
00:03:39,989 --> 00:03:44,078
They rang the bell together one more
time, and the sound spread through the

56
00:03:44,128 --> 00:03:48,111
forest, loud, round and friendly.

57
00:03:54,947 --> 00:04:00,704
Hoo, hoo, what a beautiful sound, if
fear were only a blanket in the wind,

58
00:04:00,754 --> 00:04:02,772
everybody would laugh as well,

59
00:04:02,822 --> 00:04:06,445
Popcorn said, perched on the tower ledge.

60
00:04:07,086 --> 00:04:11,702
The bell ringer gave Bruno a piece of
cake and pointed to an old castle at the

61
00:04:11,752 --> 00:04:13,014
top of the hill.

62
00:04:13,537 --> 00:04:17,376
Nobody wants to spend the night in
that castle, because a rumor says that

63
00:04:17,426 --> 00:04:21,432
things move by themselves in there, but
I think the place is only lonely and

64
00:04:21,482 --> 00:04:22,562
missing people,

65
00:04:22,612 --> 00:04:25,985
the bell ringer said, with a kind smile.

66
00:04:27,038 --> 00:04:32,321
Bruno and Popcorn climbed the hill, and
the grey-stone castle appeared among

67
00:04:32,371 --> 00:04:36,035
the trees, with the great
moon behind the towers.

68
00:04:36,192 --> 00:04:41,176
At the gate, a princess in a deep
red dress was waiting with a lantern,

69
00:04:41,276 --> 00:04:44,634
and her face looked more
tired than frightened.

70
00:04:45,177 --> 00:04:49,090
Good evening, traveler, this
used to be my family's castle,

71
00:04:49,140 --> 00:04:53,584
but everybody left because of the rumors,
and I felt so sad to see the rooms

72
00:04:53,634 --> 00:04:54,595
so empty,

73
00:04:54,645 --> 00:04:58,823
the princess said, in
a low and gentle voice.

74
00:04:59,476 --> 00:05:02,689
I do not know what fear is, and I can
stay the night here to find out what is

75
00:05:02,739 --> 00:05:03,770
really happening,

76
00:05:03,820 --> 00:05:06,567
Bruno said, steady and polite.

77
00:05:07,121 --> 00:05:10,754
If you stay, and if the strange
things do no harm to anyone,

78
00:05:10,804 --> 00:05:13,306
the castle can become a happy home again,

79
00:05:13,356 --> 00:05:16,715
the princess said, opening
the gate with care.

80
00:05:19,999 --> 00:05:25,511
Popcorn straightened the red bow and
flew ahead, lit by the moonlight.

81
00:05:26,057 --> 00:05:27,433
Hoo, hoo!

82
00:05:27,523 --> 00:05:32,707
Let us go in together, because we face
the dark better when we have company,

83
00:05:32,757 --> 00:05:37,004
Popcorn said, in a brave and gentle voice.

84
00:05:38,083 --> 00:05:42,789
In the great hall, Bruno heard a
noise of wood knocking on the floor,

85
00:05:42,861 --> 00:05:45,067
and he stopped to listen carefully.

86
00:05:46,815 --> 00:05:51,946
In the middle of the room, an orange
cat, a grey cat and a brown-haired dog

87
00:05:51,996 --> 00:05:56,057
were pushing a wooden ball against a
set of pins, as if they were playing

88
00:05:56,107 --> 00:05:58,035
skittles in the moonlight.

89
00:06:01,011 --> 00:06:04,724
The animals paused, looked at the
boy, and then went back to the game,

90
00:06:04,774 --> 00:06:09,216
because all they really wanted was
a playtime and a little company.

91
00:06:09,882 --> 00:06:13,686
So that was the terrible scary noise,
a team playing skittles in the dark?

92
00:06:13,736 --> 00:06:19,075
Bruno asked, laughing out loud with joy,
and he picked up the ball to play as

93
00:06:19,125 --> 00:06:20,325
well.

94
00:06:21,705 --> 00:06:27,049
The ball knocked down every pin, and
the cats stretched with satisfaction,

95
00:06:27,107 --> 00:06:29,563
as if they had just found a new friend.

96
00:06:31,391 --> 00:06:37,018
Hoo, hoo, I want to watch the next
game too, but with a little less noise,

97
00:06:37,068 --> 00:06:39,558
because there is another room to visit,

98
00:06:39,608 --> 00:06:43,285
Popcorn said, flapping
her wings with humor.

99
00:06:44,361 --> 00:06:49,483
In the upstairs bedroom, a large
wooden bed began to walk by itself,

100
00:06:49,597 --> 00:06:54,233
very slowly, as if it had low
wooden feet under the frame.

101
00:06:57,129 --> 00:07:01,015
Bruno climbed onto the bed, and
it took a turn around the room,

102
00:07:01,129 --> 00:07:05,904
soft and quiet, like a very
slow boat on a still lake.

103
00:07:09,490 --> 00:07:14,273
In one corner stood an old
suit of armor, still and quiet,

104
00:07:14,323 --> 00:07:18,154
and when the wind came through the
window it only swayed a little,

105
00:07:18,226 --> 00:07:20,070
as if it were saying hello.

106
00:07:29,653 --> 00:07:32,774
Good night, traveling bed,
and good night to you as well,

107
00:07:32,824 --> 00:07:34,024
iron sir!

108
00:07:34,128 --> 00:07:37,687
I still have not felt fear, but
I have felt a huge wish to laugh,

109
00:07:37,737 --> 00:07:41,109
Bruno said, lying back on the soft pillow.

110
00:07:41,700 --> 00:07:43,077
Hoo, hoo!

111
00:07:43,163 --> 00:07:48,451
This castle was not haunted, it was
only full of surprises and of forgotten

112
00:07:48,501 --> 00:07:49,413
friends,

113
00:07:49,463 --> 00:07:53,238
Popcorn said, landing on
the headboard of the bed.

114
00:07:54,337 --> 00:07:59,129
When the sun came up, the whole
castle seemed like a different place:

115
00:07:59,179 --> 00:08:04,274
the windows shone, and the courtyard
filled with the songs of little birds.

116
00:08:04,899 --> 00:08:09,474
The princess arrived in a hurry, and
the bell ringer also climbed the hill to

117
00:08:09,524 --> 00:08:11,549
see if everything was well.

118
00:08:12,166 --> 00:08:16,109
The cats and the dog were only playing,
the bed walks because it is magic and

119
00:08:16,159 --> 00:08:20,193
kind, and the armor has only been
keeping the dust off for many years,

120
00:08:20,243 --> 00:08:23,934
Bruno said, telling the
whole story with joy.

121
00:08:24,611 --> 00:08:29,477
The princess clapped her hands, happy,
and opened the hall doors to the fresh

122
00:08:29,527 --> 00:08:30,844
morning wind.

123
00:08:31,371 --> 00:08:35,271
Thank you, Bruno, now the castle
can welcome visitors again,

124
00:08:35,321 --> 00:08:37,235
and you will always be welcome here,

125
00:08:37,285 --> 00:08:40,574
the princess said, smiling with gratitude.

126
00:08:41,199 --> 00:08:46,057
Bruno felt glad, but he still
had one question in his heart.

127
00:08:46,695 --> 00:08:51,252
I helped, I laughed, I played, and even
so I still do not know what a shiver

128
00:08:51,302 --> 00:08:52,501
of fear feels like,

129
00:08:52,551 --> 00:08:55,909
Bruno said, scratching his head, puzzled.

130
00:08:56,573 --> 00:09:01,023
Popcorn exchanged a clever look with
the princess, and the two of them had an

131
00:09:01,073 --> 00:09:03,848
idea at the very same time.

132
00:09:04,945 --> 00:09:09,770
A little later, Bruno lay down for a
rest, because he had walked through the

133
00:09:09,820 --> 00:09:11,803
castle all night long.

134
00:09:12,451 --> 00:09:17,942
As soon as he closed his eyes, Popcorn
and the princess came in very slowly

135
00:09:17,992 --> 00:09:21,906
and quietly, carrying
a basin of fresh water.

136
00:09:24,797 --> 00:09:29,622
They poured the cold water carefully
over his feet, and a few little fish,

137
00:09:29,672 --> 00:09:34,420
who lived in a garden jar, swam
for a second around his ankles.

138
00:09:36,583 --> 00:09:40,630
Bruno jumped up to a sitting
position, felt his skin shiver,

139
00:09:40,680 --> 00:09:44,149
and then let out the biggest
laugh of the whole morning.

140
00:09:44,812 --> 00:09:47,863
So that was it, a shiver,
what a lovely little scare,

141
00:09:47,913 --> 00:09:49,159
and what cold water!

142
00:09:49,209 --> 00:09:54,053
Bruno said, laughing so hard that
the cats came to see the fun.

143
00:09:56,009 --> 00:09:57,386
Hoo, hoo!

144
00:09:57,497 --> 00:10:02,486
Now you know the feeling, and you have
also seen that fear grows smaller when

145
00:10:02,536 --> 00:10:05,041
we look closely and find a friend,

146
00:10:05,091 --> 00:10:08,658
Popcorn said, with her
voice full of pride.

147
00:10:09,299 --> 00:10:12,852
They had a warm breakfast in
the courtyard, with bread,

148
00:10:12,938 --> 00:10:17,407
milk and fruit, and the bell
ringer rang the bell one last time,

149
00:10:17,508 --> 00:10:18,977
just to celebrate.

150
00:10:25,783 --> 00:10:30,710
Bruno went back to the village that
same day, told his father everything,

151
00:10:30,783 --> 00:10:34,808
and promised to return to the castle
whenever his friends needed him.

152
00:10:35,455 --> 00:10:40,133
And at night, in his own bed,
the wind tapped at the window,

153
00:10:40,219 --> 00:10:44,453
Popcorn sang in a low voice,
and Bruno slept peacefully,

154
00:10:44,525 --> 00:10:48,508
already knowing that the dark
can also keep good surprises.

155
00:11:04,419 --> 00:11:05,619
The End.

156
00:11:07,327 --> 00:11:08,039
Hoo...

157
00:11:08,089 --> 00:11:09,113
Psst!

158
00:11:09,163 --> 00:11:10,735
Are you still awake?

159
00:11:10,889 --> 00:11:12,943
Did you like tonight's story?

160
00:11:13,074 --> 00:11:16,814
Bruno and Popcorn showed us
that when we look closely,

161
00:11:16,864 --> 00:11:21,866
with courage and kindness, many things
that seem scary turn into a funny

162
00:11:21,916 --> 00:11:24,946
surprise, and fear grows smaller.

163
00:11:25,206 --> 00:11:29,513
Good night, sleep tight, and
have the sweetest dreams.

164
00:11:29,809 --> 00:11:34,707
Grown-ups: if you enjoyed it,
please subscribe to Popcorn Tales,

165
00:11:34,757 --> 00:11:37,162
for more stories at bedtime.

166
00:11:37,466 --> 00:11:38,666
Hoo...

